From 681a0a574b41d6c913f03ed4203c21b184f71033 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erni Sri Satya Vennela <ernis@linux.microsoft.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 21:45:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] Drivers: hv: vmbus: don't free a channel that the rescind
 handler owns

vmbus_onoffer_rescind() looks the channel up and marks it with
channel->rescind_ref under channel_mutex, then drops the mutex and keeps
using the channel until hv_process_channel_removal() removes it.  The
err_deq_chan path of vmbus_add_channel_work() does not honour that claim:
it removes the channel from the list, unmaps the relid and frees it
regardless.  Usually the rescind handler loses the race and returns early
because relid2channel() no longer finds the channel, but if it takes
channel_mutex first it is left holding a pointer that err_deq_chan then
frees, and does a second list_del() on a poisoned entry:

  Oops: general protection fault, probably for non-canonical address
        0xdead000000000108
  Workqueue: hv_vmbus_rescind vmbus_onmessage_work
  RIP: 0010:hv_process_channel_removal+0x7d/0x230
  RAX: dead000000000122 RDX: dead000000000100
   vmbus_onoffer_rescind+0x24a/0x250
   vmbus_onmessage+0x33/0x90
   vmbus_onmessage_work+0x2a/0x40

hv_process_channel_removal() runs with channel_mutex held, so the fault
leaves the mutex locked forever and the guest stops responding entirely.
Hand the channel over instead: if rescind_ref is already set, only publish
probe_done and return, and let vmbus_onoffer_rescind() do the list
removal, the relid release and the free.  Restrict this to sub channels;
for a primary channel the rescind handler has nothing to remove it with,
because device_obj is either NULL or already gone by that point, so
handing one over would leak it rather than crash.

Fixes: e4d221b42354 ("Drivers: hv: vmbus: Resolve race condition in vmbus_onoffer_rescind()")
Signed-off-by: Erni Sri Satya Vennela <ernis@linux.microsoft.com>
---
 drivers/hv/channel_mgmt.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/hv/channel_mgmt.c b/drivers/hv/channel_mgmt.c
index c42def04ac41..bccfbd4dd664 100644
--- a/drivers/hv/channel_mgmt.c
+++ b/drivers/hv/channel_mgmt.c
@@ -577,6 +577,19 @@ static void vmbus_add_channel_work(struct work_struct *work)
 	 */
 	newchannel->probe_done = true;
 
+	/*
+	 * If vmbus_onoffer_rescind() has already claimed this channel it
+	 * removes and frees it once it observes probe_done above, so doing
+	 * that here as well would do both twice.  Only a sub channel can be
+	 * handed over: for a primary channel the rescind handler has nothing
+	 * to remove it with, because device_obj is either NULL or already
+	 * gone by this point.
+	 */
+	if (primary_channel != NULL && newchannel->rescind_ref) {
+		mutex_unlock(&vmbus_connection.channel_mutex);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	if (primary_channel == NULL)
 		list_del(&newchannel->listentry);
 	else
-- 
