From ef58f22788ba422257ce6250b669b587efa45a0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erni Sri Satya Vennela <ernis@linux.microsoft.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 21:59:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] net: hv_netvsc: do not touch queue/NAPI association
 outside sub channel setup

netvsc_sc_open() calls netif_queue_set_napi(), which requires RTNL, but
runs on the vmbus "hv_sub_chan" workqueue without taking it.  It relied on
rndis_set_subchannel() holding RTNL for the whole sub channel setup, which
no longer holds: that function now returns as soon as the device is being
rescinded, so RTNL can be dropped while netvsc_sc_open() callbacks are
still queued.  ASSERT_RTNL() does not report this, because
rtnl_is_locked() asks whether any task holds RTNL, not this one; the
per-task lockdep_rtnl_is_held() reports it on the first sub channel:

  netvsc_sc_open: netif_queue_set_napi() without RTNL held by this
  task (chn 1)
  WARNING: at netvsc_sc_open+0x191/0x1c0 [hv_netvsc]
  Workqueue: hv_sub_chan vmbus_add_channel_work

Only associate the queues while the sub channel setup is still running;
once it is not, the device is being torn down and the association is
cleared anyway.  The flag is set and cleared under RTNL, which covers
every return path out of rndis_set_subchannel().

